.Dd April 19, 2026
.Dt CMI 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmi
.Nd Capability Message Interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load at boot (required for program nonce):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo 'cmi_load="YES"' >> /boot/loader.conf
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a message-passing capability framework for kernel modules.
Capabilities are represented as file descriptors of type
.Dv DTYPE_CMI .
Each capability is an instance of a kernel service, accessed through
structured ioctls.
.Pp
The framework supports two messaging models:
.Bl -tag -width "Synchronous"
.It Sy Asynchronous
Messages are enqueued via
.Dv CMI_SENDMSG
and dequeued via
.Dv CMI_RECVMSG .
The service processes messages on a kernel taskqueue.
.It Sy Synchronous
Requests are made via
.Dv CMI_CALL .
The service handler runs in the caller's thread context.
A service is either async or sync, never both.
.El
.Pp
The device node
.Pa /dev/cmi
is created at module load with mode 0600 (root only).
.Ss Creating a capability
Open
.Pa /dev/cmi
and issue
.Dv CMI_CONNECT
with the name of the desired service.
On success, a new capability file descriptor is returned in the
.Va fd
field.
The
.Pa /dev/cmi
descriptor can then be closed.
.Ss Credential trailer
Every message carries a kernel-stamped credential trailer containing
the sender's uid, gid, jail ID, and program nonce.
The nonce is an 8-byte cryptographic random value that identifies the
program image: it is inherited across
.Xr fork 2
and rotated on
.Xr execve 2 .
Zero is never a valid nonce.
.Ss Capability control
.Bl -tag -width CMI_REVOKE_CALL
.It Dv CMI_LOCK
Prevent the capability from being passed via
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS .
One-way latch.
.It Dv CMI_REVOKE_SEND
Strip the ability to send async messages.
.It Dv CMI_REVOKE_RECV
Strip the ability to receive async messages.
.It Dv CMI_REVOKE_CALL
Strip the ability to make synchronous calls.
.It Dv CMI_TERMINATE
Kill the instance for all holders.
Subsequent operations return
.Er ECONNRESET .
.El
.Ss Introspection
.Dv CMI_GETINFO
returns the service name, badge, queue limits, and feature flags
.Pq Dv CMI_INFO_F_SENDMSG , CMI_INFO_F_CALL , CMI_INFO_F_KQUEUE .
.Ss File descriptor passing
Capabilities can carry up to 32 file descriptors per message.
Attached fds preserve their Capsicum rights through the transfer.
.Sh IOCTLS
.Bl -tag -width CMI_REVOKE_SEND
.It Dv CMI_CONNECT
Connect to a named service.
Returns a capability fd.
.It Dv CMI_SENDMSG
Send an async message with optional fd attachment.
.It Dv CMI_RECVMSG
Receive an async message.
Blocks unless
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
is set.
.It Dv CMI_CALL
Synchronous request/reply.
Returns
.Er EMSGSIZE
with the required size if the reply buffer is too small.
.It Dv CMI_GETINFO
Query capability metadata.
.It Dv CMI_LOCK
Prevent SCM_RIGHTS delegation.
.It Dv CMI_REVOKE_SEND , CMI_REVOKE_RECV , CMI_REVOKE_CALL
Strip specific abilities.
.It Dv CMI_TERMINATE
Kill the instance.
.El
.Sh SERVICES
The following services are provided as loadable kernel modules:
.Bl -tag -width cmi_kernelstore
.It Sy cmi_debug
Process debug protection via MACF.
Shield a program from ptrace and most signals.
Mint debug tokens to authorize specific debuggers.
SIGKILL and SIGCONT are always allowed.
.It Sy cmi_token
Kernel-gated authorization tokens.
Create labeled tokens, validate, and revoke.
.It Sy cmi_namespace
Namespace management backed by FreeBSD jails.
Create, enter, and remove namespaces.
.It Sy cmi_kernelstore
Shared key-value store.
The capability fd is the credential.
Owner can mint member fds to share access.
256 keys max, 4096 bytes per value.
.It Sy cmi_pair
Bidirectional capability pair for peer-to-peer messaging.
.El
.Sh LIMITS
.Bl -tag -width CMI_MSG_PAYLOAD_SIZE
.It Dv CMI_MAX_MSG
14336 bytes (14 KB) maximum usable payload per message.
.It Dv CMI_MAX_FDS
32 file descriptors per message.
.It Dv CMI_DEFAULT_QUEUE_DEPTH
256 messages per async queue (configurable by service).
.El
.Pp
Messages are fixed at 16384 bytes (4 pages) including a 2048-byte
header reserved for framework use.
Sync-only services do not allocate message queues.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width kern.cmi.instances
.It Va kern.cmi.services
Number of registered services.
.It Va kern.cmi.instances
Number of active capability instances.
.El
.Sh DTRACE PROBES
The
.Nm
provider defines the following probes:
.Pp
connect, send, recv, dispatch, reply, notify, call, revoke, close.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/cmi
.It Pa /dev/cmi
Control device for creating capabilities.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
RX queue full (SENDMSG), or no message available with
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
(RECVMSG).
.It Bq Er EACCES
Operation revoked via
.Dv CMI_REVOKE_* .
.It Bq Er ECONNRESET
Instance terminated.
.It Bq Er EMSGSIZE
Payload too large (SENDMSG), or reply buffer too small
(RECVMSG, CALL).
The required size is returned in the length field.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
Service not found (CONNECT).
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
Wrong messaging model for this service.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr mac 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
framework first appeared in
.Fx 15.0
as part of 5BSD.
